        {
          "type": "text",
          "duration": 190,
          "text": {
            "en_us": "Your opponent starts with 3 health and you start with 4. Each action has a fixed 17-second limit; timing out automatically shoots yourself. Each supply rolls 2–5 items, multiplies by 70% and rounds to 1–4. Only the initial supply then subtracts 1 per player, never below 0: your opponent starts with 0–3 items, while your preserved extra initial item gives you 1–4. Later supplies remain 1–4 each, with no further subtraction or Devil bonus. Carried plus pending items are capped at 8 per player; full backpacks queue supplies and existing items stay. Duels use a separate inventory, restored afterward. Your opponent is never executed for losing a duel. When you lose, you consume one defeat allowance and return to the train; you have max(1, floor(actual starting participants / 8)) allowances, and only after they are exhausted does your loss truly kill you. Every duel loser gains a random Disabled Patient symptom for 3 minutes.",
